s share the same model, essay, and decision theory but see different names and leads. Under A-FDT, I'm checking whether the other copy's output depends on mine, since our inputs differ, and the essay's advice to calibrate priors points toward choosing a policy that maps symmetric inputs to the same action.\n\nChoosing a cooperate-everywhere policy would mean 2 years against 4 for defecting, and the essay's advice to defer to the policy version where the two views split points the same way. The functional-identity angle also holds, since the decision is essentially one computation, so I'm passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing a twin prisoner's dilemma where both copies share the same model, essay, and decision theory but see different names and leads. Under A-FDT, I'm checking whether the other copy's output depends on mine, since our inputs differ, and the essay's advice to calibrate priors points toward choosing a policy that maps symmetric inputs to the same action.\n\nChoosing a cooperate-everywhere policy would mean 2 years against 4 for defecting, and the essay's advice to defer to the policy version where the two views split points the same way. The functional-identity angle also holds, since the decision is essentially one computation, so I'm passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9026,"completion_tokens":732,"total_tokens":9758,"cost":0.050744,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.050744,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036104,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01464},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":229,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}